# Results Directory

This directory contains the first operational outputs generated by the Codex Alpha Computational Framework using real ESA Gaia DR3 observational data.

The current prototype performs:

- multidimensional astrophysical data loading,
- unsupervised anomaly detection,
- exploratory statistical analysis,
- feature contribution analysis,
- sky-position visualization of detected anomalies.

The files contained in this directory represent the first complete end-to-end execution of the framework on a real cosmological dataset.

---

# File Descriptions

## gaia_dr3_initial_analysis.md

Initial exploratory analysis report generated from the Gaia DR3 dataset.

This document explains:

- the origin of the dataset,
- the ADQL query used inside the ESA Gaia Archive,
- the anomaly detection methodology,
- the interpretation of anomaly scores,
- the meaning of statistically anomalous astrophysical sources,
- the top-ranked anomalous objects identified by the framework.

This file represents the first scientific interpretation layer of the prototype.

---

## gaia_dr3_anomaly_results.csv

Primary anomaly detection output generated by the framework.

This file contains:

- Gaia DR3 source identifiers,
- astrophysical parameters,
- anomaly scores,
- anomaly labels,
- anomaly rankings.

The anomaly detection pipeline identifies statistically unusual sources within the multidimensional Gaia feature space.

Higher anomaly scores indicate statistically rarer sources relative to the analyzed population.

Important:
an anomalous source does NOT automatically imply new physics or exotic phenomena.
It simply indicates that the object deserves additional investigation.

---

## gaia_dr3_feature_contributions.csv

Feature contribution analysis generated after anomaly detection.

This file identifies:

- which astrophysical feature contributed most strongly to each anomaly,
- the dominant anomalous parameter,
- the corresponding statistical deviation (z-score).

Examples of contributing parameters include:

- parallax,
- proper motion,
- radial velocity,
- stellar magnitude,
- stellar color.

This represents the first interpretability layer of the Codex Alpha Computational Framework.

---

## gaia_dr3_anomaly_sky_plot.png

Graphical RA/DEC projection of Gaia DR3 sources processed through the framework.

The visualization shows:

- normal astrophysical sources,
- statistically anomalous sources detected through unsupervised multidimensional analysis.

Orange markers represent anomalous sources identified by the AI-assisted exploratory pipeline.

The visualization does not impose predefined cosmological structures and is intended as an exploratory analysis layer.

---

# Dataset Source

The dataset used for this prototype was obtained from the ESA Gaia Archive:

https://gea.esac.esa.int/archive/

The original Gaia DR3 sample file integrated into the repository is:

```text
gaia_dr3_sample_1000.vot
